{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>נפתולי אלהים נפתלתי.</b> Like נפתלי, meaning: I suffered great distress with my sister and gathered strength to bear my suffering until now. Another explanation: the language of עקש ופתלתל, meaning: I was entwined in stubbornness with my sister, for I was barren, and now I can as well, now that I have sons like her. Another explanation: the language of צמיד פתיל, meaning: bonds of the Name — I became bound with my sister, for from my sister's sons Betzalel is destined to emerge, who was filled with the spirit of wisdom, as it is said: ״ובצלאל בן אורי בן חור למטה יהודה״ and ״ואמלא אותו רוח אלהים״. And I became bound with my sister in that same craft, for it is written: ״ואתו אהליאב בן אחיסמך למטה דן״. I could as well in the First Temple that Solomon built, which Huram completed, who was from the tribe of Naftali."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:20.557622049Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}